      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The maximum recommended daily dose is 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg for extended-release in the US. At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a transcription or unit error. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), which is the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- A typical starting dose of **500 mg twice daily** or **850 mg once daily** with a meal, titrated up over weeks.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your resident or attending. Once you have the dose, give me the dose, frequency, and formulation (IR or ER), and I'll enter it right away. If the dose really is 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that with your supervising physician first. I'd also add a note to the order documenting that they approved it."
      }
     ],
